.TITLE "umount"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Detaches a mounted filesystem from the directory hierarchy. it ensures that all __pending data__ is written to the disk before the device is safely removed.

.DIV "TLDR"
**umount path**
Unmounts the filesystem attached to a specific directory or device.
> __path__ the mount point or device name

**umount -l path**
Performs a lazy unmount, detaching the filesystem as soon as it is no longer busy.
> __-l__ lazy flag | __path__ the mount point

**umount -f path**
Forcefully unmounts a filesystem, which is useful for unreachable network drives.
> __-f__ force flag | __path__ the mount point

.DIV "SUMMARY"
If you receive a "device is busy" error, it means a program or shell is currently using a file on that drive. You must close those programs or navigate out of the directory before you can successfully run __umount__.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:mount**

documentation: __https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man8/umount.8.html__
